invariant: INV-16
file: p256_wide_mul.c
catches: p256_equiv_test
reason: multiple_select starts its scan at the second of the eight
  multiples of the point, so a digit of size 1 selects nothing and
  p256_wide_mul adds all-zero coordinates in place of the point itself.
  Every other digit is right, so one window in eight is wrong for a
  random scalar. bin/p256_equiv_test holds the multiplication to
  p256_point_mul on scalars whose windows hold every digit, and
  proof/p256_wide_digit_harness.c proves the scan returns the multiple at
  every index.

